Z||000001||DRH||01-12-2000||05:14 PM||||Here are a couple of sites to check out...<P> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gene-down/project.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gene-down/project.htm</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.netvista.net/~jlatteri/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.netvista.net/~jlatteri/</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.terranexus.com/fieroman/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.terranexus.com/fieroman/</A>   (Not an SC but very detailed, click on the  link in the Engine Swap Details paragraph)<P>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-12-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||01-12-2000||05:16 PM||||Plan on about $6k and 100 hrs. Better and cheaper is to have someone that knows what they're doing perform the swap. I would recommend ACE.(Guess who did mine) <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||88GT||01-13-2000||12:02 AM||||Chris West of West Coast Fiero's has a good site.  He outlines what it will take and the estimated cost of each part change needed.  his address is: <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/Engines/Engines.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/Engines/Engines.html</A> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||01-13-2000||04:19 AM||||I did a 3.8 with ace kit, but mine is not supercharged after 1600 for the engine and tranny with 50k miles on it from a wrecking yard and 1500 for the kit and about 100 or so in miscaleneous parts i WOULD SAY 3,200 to 3,300 and about 3 days to get the motor and stuff in and work out bugs.  It depends also on how effecient you are in taking out the  whole drive train (the motor, tranny, craddle) the better you are at taking that stuff out and putting it back in the faster the install will go.||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||01-13-2000||11:29 AM||||jihuber, you'll want to talk to Curry Obenshain, he runs Fiero Owners Club of Southeast Virginia. He is in the process of installing a 3.8SC in his 86SE. According to the last newsletter, Curry, and several other club members, have installed the clutch, flywheel, and transmission (Getrag 5-spd) to the engine. By now they may have it on the cradle. <BR>If I remember right, he paid $3100 for the engine with 2,800 miles from a Grand Prix GTP. He's been working on this for over a year, mainly once or twice a month with club members. He's taking his time and doing it right!<P>For some reason, the thinks it will beat my turbo-charged 86SE!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>LMK if you want Curry's email, I have it somewhere....<BR>Good luck!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||jlhuber||01-13-2000||01:11 PM||||turbo, if you could find his address that would be great.  I am located in New Jersey near Philadelphia, and I want to take a few trips to some clubs and shows on the east coast this summer.  I might have to stop by and see him sometime.<BR>                        TIA<BR>                         -Jess||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||01-15-2000||11:35 AM||||I think Bob Steiger Twin Lakes Fiero has done 3800 sc swaps.  He's in Paxton Ill (217)379 9140.<P>I have a 3800 sc in my Buick, and it goes like a bat out of .... I can't even think what kind of performance that engine would deliver in a Fiero.   If I did that swap, I'd upgrade the brakes.<P>He does 3.4 crate engine swaps routinely.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||01-16-2000||01:15 AM||||Not in a Fiero, but a Ciera GT. I keep looking at the Fiero with that glazed look in my eyes. I'm considering it. Both the DOHC and SC have their issues.||||reg||1
